heat-dashboard for Ubuntu
--------------------------

The heat-dashboard package handles xstatic dependencies similar how the horizon
package does.

These dependencies are bundled up alongside the upstream release tarball and are
included in the python3-heat-dashboard package under heat_dashboard.xstatic.

To refresh the orig-xstatic.tar.gz run:

    ./debian/rules refresh-xstatic

this will use pip to retrieve all xstatic assets detailed in requirements.txt
and bundle them into an additional 'upstream' tar.gz, leveraging the multi-orig
feature of source format 3.0.

The refresh-xstatic rule also extracts the xstatic assets into ./xstatic/
directory of the source package. This allows for patching of xstatic files
before they are copied into the python3-heat-dashboard package. For example:

    quilt edit ./xstatic/pkg/angular_uuid/data/angular-uuid.js
